<div class="block-content block-content--type-basic block-content--38961 block-content--view-mode-full">
  
  
  <div class="block-content__content">
    
            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"><div class="accordion accordion-items-stay-open" data-accordion-id="e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f" id="accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f"><div class="accordion-item"><div class="accordion-header"><a class="accordion-button collapsed" href="#accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f-1" role="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f-1">Fall 2026 Dates and Deadlines</a></div><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f-1"><div class="accordion-body"><table class="table"><caption>Fall 2026 Overview</caption><thead><tr><th>COURSE TERM</th><th>FULL SEMESTER</th><th>1ST HALF</th><th>2ND HALF</th><th>1ST MINI</th><th>2ND MINI</th><th>3RD MINI</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>START DATE</th><td>August 24</td><td>August 24</td><td>October 19</td><td>August 24</td><td>September 30</td><td>November 6</td></tr><tr><th>Last Day to Add without Signatures [1]</th><td>August 30</td><td>August 23</td><td>October 18</td><td>August 23</td><td>September 29</td><td>November 5</td></tr><tr><th>Schedule Adjustment [2] and Elect Pass/Fail</th><td>August 30</td><td>August 30</td><td>October 22</td><td>August 30</td><td>Day following 2nd Class</td><td>Day following 2nd Class</td></tr><tr><th>Last Day to ADD [3]</th><td>September 4</td><td>September 4</td><td>Day following 3rd Class</td><td>Day following 3rd Class</td><td>Day following 3rd Class</td><td>Day following 3rd Class</td></tr><tr><th>Last Day to DROP with &ldquo;W&rdquo; [4]</th><td>November 5</td><td>September 29</td><td>November 30</td><td>September 16</td><td>October 23</td><td>December 7</td></tr><tr><th>P/F change to Letter</th><td>November 5</td><td>September 29</td><td>November 30</td><td>September 16</td><td>October 23</td><td>December 7</td></tr><tr><th>End DATE</th><td>December 18</td><td>October 16</td><td>December 18</td><td>September 29</td><td>November 5</td><td>December 18</td></tr></tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span class="small-type">[1] Signatures are required to add a course after this date.<br>[2] After these dates, late fees apply ($20.00) for all schedule changes and &ldquo;W&rdquo; grades are assigned for drops.<br>[3] You MUST be registered in courses by this date in order to receive credit and grades.<br>[4] For Withdrawal from the university, go to the Student Affairs Office.</span></p><p><em>SUNY Oneonta reserves the right to cancel any course because of insufficient enrollment or other reasons. Should cancellation be necessary, a student may choose another course or request a full refund.</em></p><h3>Fall 2026 Details by Month</h3><h4>AUGUST</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="ee2fd51d3071377796e20c25e8cf68861"><strong>19-22 Wednesday-Saturday</strong>: <a href="/admissions/admitted-students/orientation" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="969556f7-2be3-443a-9359-a1ac3b7c11d1" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Orientation">New student arrival and orientation</a>.</li><li data-list-item-id="e2de1027da6ed613f6e15ec84497e0eff"><strong>23 Sunday</strong>: Last day to register. Any student who has not registered by this date at 3:00 pm will be assessed a $40 Late Registration Fee.</li><li data-list-item-id="ec0a5fd5d08188404667c2f6563f21210"><strong>24 Monday</strong>: Classes Begin<ul><li data-list-item-id="e67505cd7208bb754778e90979fb1e894">Add/Drop begins online and in the Registrar&rsquo;s Office.</li></ul></li><li class="ck-list-marker-bold" data-list-item-id="e90b24dc321ce1851743cb944abe8ece4"><strong>30 Sunday: **ADD/DROP Ends**</strong><ul><li data-list-item-id="e0ff8bf0e71073f1740e702337a0b162d">After this date, all schedule adjustments (add/drop) for full semester courses will result in a $20 late fee.</li><li data-list-item-id="ef9844c09a012d03137f8bc7d81289a44">&ldquo;W&rdquo; grades are assigned for dropping a full semester course after this date.</li><li data-list-item-id="e1f3491db089995aeb4becd7d80a87042">After this date, all Individual Course Enrollment, Independent Study, Internship and Teaching Assistantship forms (3 s.h. or more) will result in a $20 late fee.</li><li data-list-item-id="e20342f9b653bd63de7754cdeaf63fe77">Last day for students with part-time enrollment to drop a course with no tuition liability.</li></ul></li></ul><h4>SEPTEMBER</h4><ul><li class="ck-list-marker-bold" data-list-item-id="eeb47dfc63b955d938d63a7fc0e6994fc"><strong>4 Friday: **LAST DAY TO ADD A FULL SEMESTER COURSE**</strong><ul><li data-list-item-id="e43bd504434e1dfba54a13b74360f4692">You MUST be registered in a course by this date to receive credit and grades. See chart above for mini and half-semester ADD/DROP deadlines.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="e0586590c958b3262309aedec853eb323"><strong>7 Monday</strong>:<ul><li data-list-item-id="ee592959d71351abb269964ee3a332c06">Labor Day. No classes.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="e19d0f2aefe2642185a631c901782a2b2"><strong>21 Monday</strong>:<ul><li data-list-item-id="e54d82f80bc70e68a8f38614c2ef8c052">Semester bill - second Installment Plan payment due.</li><li data-list-item-id="e8caef2972ed8c70fd5ed2aeb609f9d02">Grow, Thrive, Live Day</li><li data-list-item-id="edfea25dafd822b6bdf4ec877f47c8f0b">TAP Certification begins. Students receiving TAP awards must be in full-time DAC (12 s.h. or more of Degree Applicable Credit) to be eligible for TAP. Failure to enroll in full-time DAC will result in the loss of the award.</li></ul></li></ul><h4>OCTOBER</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="e0cd438a17110907186455a88018a1509"><strong>15 Thursday</strong>: Grow, Thrive, Live Day</li><li data-list-item-id="e690583b914887ae5ac2a6104bd82bb48"><strong>21 Wednesday</strong>: Semester bill - third and final Installment Plan payment due.</li><li data-list-item-id="e433dbd45e7edd1f22ad1164b49493536"><strong>22 Thursday</strong>: Interim Progress Reports due from faculty.</li></ul><h4>NOVEMBER</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="ebfd33627077c5c1dad1f6601a35c6871"><strong>2 Monday</strong>:<ul><li data-list-item-id="e6b40d77084804e0d9af79b5d807f1c2c">Beginning date for Winter 2027 pre-enrollment.</li><li data-list-item-id="eac76c35d8e7cde3cf67fb1f3a380b203">December 2026 Diploma/Certificate Application and related application fee due in the Registrar&rsquo;s Office.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="eb6517217fcfca75912a6d57192dcdffd"><strong>3 Tuesday</strong>: Grow, Thrive, Live Day</li><li class="ck-list-marker-bold" data-list-item-id="e9d6224b55c352f5d9af29431f74ae755"><strong>5 Thursday: **WITHDRAWAL DEADLINE**</strong><ul><li data-list-item-id="e0e44ce557de22c43ce1602e3c3d31856">Last day to drop a full semester course.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="e8237501ee95b93626dfdf0292e8a72b6"><strong>9 Monday</strong>: After this date, all Individual Course Enrollment, Independent Study, Internship and Teaching Assistantship forms (less than 3 s.h.) will result in a $20 late fee.</li><li data-list-item-id="e1829063ad70058d8c7fa51f13ac39341"><strong>11 Wednesday</strong>: Last day for students to make up Incomplete and Pending Grades from Spring and Summer 2026 or to file the Extension of Time Form.</li><li data-list-item-id="e2bd827a786ab806e3398753470a2d9bf"><strong>16 Monday</strong>: Beginning date for Spring 2027 pre-enrollment.</li><li data-list-item-id="e19c19ee1644d52a98e6f87798e7d41ce"><strong>20 Friday</strong>: University closes after last class.</li><li data-list-item-id="eb13570916a7ee4a1f8bc8f97cb1a9c7d"><strong>30 Monday</strong>: Classes resume.<ul><li data-list-item-id="ec1dc40df3c72f0508336118ea6d5e10f">Last day to withdraw or take a leave of absence from the University. After this date, students must complete all coursework.</li><li data-list-item-id="eb1855a7b5bc8baa0a34bebfa157c426f">Last day for faculty to turn in grades for previously assigned Incomplete Grades or to file an Extension of Time Form.</li></ul></li></ul><h4>DECEMBER</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="e68e738187c973f44aebf1fbe3dcc100e"><strong>9 Wednesday</strong>: Will follow a Monday class schedule.</li><li data-list-item-id="ece9e775c80aff9f88c68f6470ffdd771"><strong>13 Sunday</strong>: Commencement.</li><li data-list-item-id="e83c520a8d3bfb6d4bf27d0a13e1f64e4"><strong>11 Friday</strong>: Study Day.</li><li data-list-item-id="e54e5704fbcd8f7e3b4fec515d8842d8f"><strong>14-18 Monday through Friday</strong>: Finals Week. Special schedule, see reverse.</li></ul><hr><h3>Add Full Semester Courses online from August 24 at 8 a.m. until August 30 at Midnight</h3><p>No signatures required for course drops/withdrawals. These can be processed online until the withdrawal dates for each part of term.</p><p>No signatures required for course adds from August 24th &ndash; August 30th, UNLESS:</p><ul><li data-list-item-id="e1b8eaef1e5b234b9a5cd9602e5d3d543">The course is a <strong>First Mini</strong> or <strong>First Half Semester Course</strong>.</li><li data-list-item-id="e4e35c0dbe48f4ee6fd53308b32984ad3">The course requires department or instructor approval.</li><li data-list-item-id="e053cc993b30d4a764c52b8eff42cc15b">The course is reserved for students in a designated major.</li><li data-list-item-id="ecd80cf24e219b2b3ad8adf925a5320b5">You have not met the course prerequisite.</li><li data-list-item-id="e91a85d165a76f2b4bf635206a5bacd26">You have a time conflict.</li></ul><p>Students with any of the above problems <strong>MUST</strong> process add/drops via the Registrar&rsquo;s Office. All schedule adjustments for full semester courses made after February 1st at midnight require the instructor&rsquo;s permission.</p><p>Note: An instructor adding a name to or deleting a student name from a roster does NOT CONSTITUTE an official add or drop. <strong>Students are academically responsible for making all schedule adjustments either on the web or via the Registrar&rsquo;s Office. Students should always check their schedules carefully.</strong></p></div></div></div><div class="accordion-item"><div class="accordion-header"><a class="accordion-button collapsed" href="#accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f-2" role="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f-2">Fall 2026 Final Exam Schedule</a></div><div class="accordion-collapse collapse" id="accordion-e7986a1d55a89e57b18986225f9e6491f-2"><div class="accordion-body"><p>During the last week of the semester, day classes will meet for 2 1/2 hour periods according to the schedule below.</p><p>These periods are to be used for instruction and/or examination.</p><table class="table"><caption>Final Exam Week Class Schedule, December 14 - December 18, 2026</caption><thead><tr><th>DATE AND TIME</th><th>Monday<br>DECEMBER 14</th><th>Tuesday<br>DECEMBER 15</th><th>Wednesday<br>DECEMBER 16</th><th>Thursday<br>DECEMBER 17</th><th>Friday<br>DECEMBER 18</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>8:00 A.M.&ndash;10:30 a.m.</th><td>8 MWF</td><td>8:30 Tu Th</td><td>9 MWF</td><td>10 Tu Th</td><td>10 MWF</td></tr><tr><th>11:00 a.m.&ndash;1:30 p.m.</th><td>11 MWF</td><td>11:30 Tu Th</td><td>12 MWF</td><td>1 Tu Th</td><td>1 MWF</td></tr><tr><th>2:00 p.m.&ndash;4:30 p.m.</th><td>2 MWF</td><td>2:30 Tu Th</td><td>4 MW</td><td>4 Tu Th</td><td>--</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Note: All one-day-a-week evening classes (Starting at 5:00 pm or later only) will meet at their regularly scheduled times.</p><p><strong>Instructions for determining when your final exam is scheduled:</strong></p><ul><li data-list-item-id="e6daa009de5aa8b475e3ff30534ab171f">Final Exam times are determined by the meeting time of your class. For example, if your class meets 10 Tu Th your final exam will be on Thursday, December 17 from 8:00 to 10:30am. Courses with labs are scheduled based on the lecture time of the course.</li><li data-list-item-id="e8ad0f364751e786f6ba407cfc6768379">Courses which do not follow a standard time pattern are scheduled based on the initial schedule time of the course. For example, a course which is scheduled to meet at 2 on WThF has an initial meeting time of 2W. The only 2W on the chart is on Monday, December 14. Therefore, the final for a course which meets 2 WThF is scheduled for Monday, December 14 from 2:00 to 4:30pm.</li><li data-list-item-id="ef2bc5b49bb800623c905299630a9851f">Final Exams for in-person classes are held in regularly assigned rooms.</li></ul><p><strong>Students should consult the Finals Week schedule to avoid enrolling in courses which would cause them to have multiple examinations on the same day.</strong></p></div></div></div></div></div>
      
  </div>
</div>

    </div>
  </div>



