    <div class="accordion accordion-items-stay-open" id="accordion-67181">
                              <div class="accordion-item">
          <p class="accordion-header" id="heading-67181--1">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-67181--1" aria-controls="collapse-67181--1">
              <div class="title">
                <span class="p">Spring 2027 Dates and Deadlines</span>
                              </div>
            </button>
          </p>
          <div id="collapse-67181--1" class="accordion-collapse collapse " aria-labelledby="heading-67181--1" data-bs-parent_="#accordion-67181">
            <div class="accordion-body">

                            <div>
               <table class="table"><caption>Spring 2026 Overview</caption><thead><tr><th>COURSE TERM</th><th>FULL SEMESTER</th><th>1ST HALF</th><th>2ND HALF</th><th>1ST MINI</th><th>2ND MINI</th><th>3RD MINI</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>START DATE</th><td>January 25</td><td>January 25</td><td>March 29</td><td>January 25</td><td>March 2</td><td>April 14</td></tr><tr><th>Last Day to Add without Signatures [1]</th><td>January 31</td><td>January 24</td><td>March 28</td><td>January 24</td><td>March 1</td><td>April 13</td></tr><tr><th>Schedule Adjustment [2] and Elect Pass/Fail</th><td>January 31</td><td>January 31</td><td>April 1</td><td>January 31</td><td>Day following 2nd Class</td><td>Day following 2nd Class</td></tr><tr><th>Last Day to ADD [3]</th><td>February 5</td><td>February 5</td><td>Day following 3rd Class</td><td>Day following 3rd Class</td><td>Day following 3rd Class</td><td>Day following 3rd Class</td></tr><tr><th>Last Day to DROP with &ldquo;W&rdquo; [4]</th><td>April 13</td><td>March 1</td><td>May 5</td><td>February 17</td><td>April 1</td><td>May 2</td></tr><tr><th>P/F change to Letter</th><td>April 13</td><td>March 1</td><td>May 5</td><td>February 17</td><td>April 1</td><td>May2</td></tr><tr><th>End DATE</th><td>May 21</td><td>March 19</td><td>May 21</td><td>March 1</td><td>April 13</td><td>May 21</td></tr></tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span class="small-type">[1] Signatures are required to add a course after this date.<br>[2] After these dates, late fees apply ($20.00) for all schedule changes and &ldquo;W&rdquo; grades are assigned for drops.<br>[3] You MUST be registered in courses by this date in order to receive credit and grades.<br>[4] For Withdrawal from the university, go to the Student Affairs Office, Sherman Hall.</span></p><p><em>SUNY Oneonta reserves the right to cancel any course because of insufficient enrollment or other reasons. Should cancellation be necessary, a student may choose another course or request a full refund.</em></p><h3>Spring 2027 Details by Month</h3><h4>January</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="e465d2f6c3732720584c9f639bf09bc87"><strong>22-23 Thursday-Saturday</strong>: New Student arrival and orientation.</li><li data-list-item-id="e22d396e455060cb0b674fef94aed8bbc"><strong>24 Sunday</strong>: Last day to register. Any student who has not registered by this date will be assessed a $40 Late Registration Fee.</li><li class="ck-list-marker-bold" data-list-item-id="ea4cc5365812afd01f94e96871c0d8003"><strong>25 Monday: Classes Begin</strong><ul><li data-list-item-id="e0bd38c74bff986ee89a4ec195e51afb5">Add/Drop begins online and in the Registrar&rsquo;s Office.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="e8860181a9d08d06f8b5fcd8dcea74b33"><strong>31 Sunday</strong>: **ADD/DROP Ends**<ul><li data-list-item-id="e2ec716f07ce1723834354e087bedbf41">After this date, all schedule adjustments (add/drop) for full semester courses will result in a $20 late fee.</li><li data-list-item-id="e16e42667e40dee33ea673716764a921a">&ldquo;W&rdquo; grades are assigned for dropping a full semester course after this date.</li><li data-list-item-id="e972309f59aaa87c2df59a637f56c9801">After this date, all Individual Course Enrollment, Independent Study, Internship, and Teaching Assistantship forms (3 s.h. or more) will result in a</li><li data-list-item-id="e9ac28f131697375ddb67216916732c78">$20 late fee.</li><li data-list-item-id="e22df76f2cd00ad87110eeb402d320f50">Last day for students with part-time enrollment to drop a course with no tuition liability.</li></ul></li></ul><h4>February</h4><ul><li class="ck-list-marker-bold" data-list-item-id="e7dbda68f5b92c13bbfffeb97835cdbec"><strong>5 Friday: **LAST DAY TO ADD A FULL SEMESTER COURSE**</strong><ul><li data-list-item-id="e93fd1f95133a0fe83f567848cea53c26">You MUST be registered in a course by this date to receive credit and grades. See chart above for mini and half-semester ADD/DROP deadlines.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="e01c8444c4f4f6dbeea68c62700c8dca4"><strong>8 Monday</strong>: Grow. Thrive. Live. Day</li><li data-list-item-id="e4fd648249eb083d4dd962e35b0d7a514"><strong>21 Sunday</strong>: Semester bill: second Installment Plan payment due.</li><li data-list-item-id="e2558219644a01f23b9c22bf174e10e7e"><strong>22 Monday</strong>: TAP Certification begins. Students receiving TAP awards must be in full-time DAC (12 s.h. or more of Degree Applicable Credit) to be eligible for TAP. Failure to enroll in full-time DAC will result in the loss of the award.</li></ul><h4>March</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="e72bce4a68a92a1ca6ccf77423c56ba63"><strong>1 Monday</strong>: Summer session registration begins.</li><li data-list-item-id="e3e65dc7a9655c401c81ff40dd1bebfae"><strong>10 Wednesday</strong>: Grow. Thrive. Live. Day</li><li data-list-item-id="e669c010e7a0d26d83ef7588debed1741"><strong>19 Friday</strong>: University closes after last class.</li><li data-list-item-id="e981234b5023d7a400a4329841961a027"><strong>21 Sunday</strong>: Semester bill: third and final Installment Plan payment due.</li><li data-list-item-id="e0f33560acde635c7d055575f0f1faf62"><strong>29 Monday</strong>: Classes resume.</li><li data-list-item-id="ec32eef89b04b8cdabef1642d0ea7dbee"><strong>30 Tuesday</strong>: Interim Progress Reports due from faculty.</li></ul><h4>April</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="e6be6647f34cde7fd03d8e582a763e918"><strong>1 Thursday</strong>:<ul><li data-list-item-id="e17a7e50208b32b28bd77c935158e88e4">Students graduating in May or August 2027 must file a Diploma/Certificate Application and related application fee in the Registrar&rsquo;s Office - Sherman Hall.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="e432e77709df70f6f2be9724070224647"><strong>12 Monday:</strong> Beginning date for Fall 2027 pre-enrollment.</li><li data-list-item-id="ed6b67294eacda03b1580f7d257f8cd97"><strong>13 Tuesday</strong>: <strong>**WITHDRAWAL DEADLINE**</strong><ul><li data-list-item-id="e7d400f921223a74b59617241b783c7f1">Last day to drop a full semester course.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="ecee91747b81d0a6eaa4a47cd9a5ca9b1"><strong>14 Wednesday</strong>: Last day for faculty to turn in grades for previously assigned Incomplete Grades or to file an Extension of Time Form.<ul><li data-list-item-id="e693cc5b3a17ee9d1b8579a2ff327d9b2">After this date, all Individual Course Enrollment, Independent Study, Internship, and Teaching Assistantship forms (less than 3 s.h.) will result in a $20 late fee.</li></ul></li><li data-list-item-id="e3e43ec53c6154374993c42bfec4d70f8"><strong>21 Wednesday</strong>: Last day for students to make up Incomplete and Pending Grades from Fall 2026 and Winter 2027 or to file the Extension of Time Form.</li><li data-list-item-id="e51ecb586b6d66cd6592cce12f67e5def"><strong>22 Thursday</strong>: Grow. Thrive. Live. Day</li><li data-list-item-id="eed506fc4719d8752c6d5f57b8fc56dc5"><strong>23 Friday</strong>: Grow. Thrive. Live. Day</li></ul><h4>May</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="e15bea18cddd3aac0dbc99739ac9e15c6"><strong>3 Monday</strong>: Last day to withdraw or take a leave of absence from the University. After this date, students must complete all coursework.</li><li data-list-item-id="e25b8fecc324907e22ce885045e703ae4"><strong>4 Tuesday</strong>: Grow. Thrive. Live. Day</li><li data-list-item-id="e8d60d127163f668c01cab93dbe0bf472"><strong>5 Wednesday</strong>: Last day for faculty to turn in grades for previously assigned Incomplete and Pending Grades or to file an Extension of Time Form.</li><li data-list-item-id="e98f9c683d2d4f30486ffee7f8474c954"><strong>14 Friday</strong>: Last day of regular class schedule.</li><li data-list-item-id="ed73e8d3908f7b80af3c26847622d33d6"><strong>17-21 Monday through Friday</strong>: Finals Week. Special schedule, see below.</li><li data-list-item-id="efd9787375180a1b3a3758c1b6a6c7649"><strong>21 Friday</strong>: Graduate Degree Commencement</li><li data-list-item-id="e463adbb81cd71a20996dab35a12322ee"><strong>22 Saturday</strong>: Undergraduate Degree Commencement</li></ul><hr><h3>Add Full Semester Courses online from Jan. 25 at 8 a.m. until Jan. 31 at Midnight</h3><p>No signatures required for course drops/withdrawals. These can be processed online until the withdrawal dates for each part of term.</p><p>No signatures required for course adds from January 25th &ndash; January 31st, UNLESS:</p><ul><li data-list-item-id="e3bfee4b7000dba82d8e61c8a88fa91f0">The course is a <strong>First Mini</strong> or <strong>First Half Semester Course</strong>.</li><li data-list-item-id="e7749f6f6adc472990f5f482a1bdd81fb">The course requires department or instructor approval.</li><li data-list-item-id="e3f960655f24cc67ff483656b79f51ef2">The course is reserved for students in a designated major.</li><li data-list-item-id="e7aea97a6daf0069d9f3adea3f25dfe4d">You have not met the course prerequisite.</li><li data-list-item-id="ebbd418c57a078945f86dea2dbfbc817a">You have a time conflict.</li></ul><p>Students with any of the above problems <strong>MUST</strong> process add/drops via the Registrar&rsquo;s Office. All schedule adjustments for full semester courses made after February 1st at midnight require the instructor&rsquo;s permission.</p><p>Note: An instructor adding a name to or deleting a student name from a roster does NOT CONSTITUTE an official add or drop. Students are academically responsible for making all schedule adjustments either on the web or via the Registrar&rsquo;s Office. Students should always check their schedules carefully.</p>
              </div>
              
              <div class="d-flex gap-2 justify-content-start align-items-center my-1">
                            </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
                              <div class="accordion-item">
          <p class="accordion-header" id="heading-67181--2">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-67181--2" aria-controls="collapse-67181--2">
              <div class="title">
                <span class="p">Spring 2027 Final Exam Schedule</span>
                              </div>
            </button>
          </p>
          <div id="collapse-67181--2" class="accordion-collapse collapse " aria-labelledby="heading-67181--2" data-bs-parent_="#accordion-67181">
            <div class="accordion-body">

                            <div>
               <p>During the last week of the semester, day classes will meet for 2 1/2 hour periods according to the schedule below. These periods are to be used for instruction and/or examination.</p><table class="table table-style-align-center"><caption>Final Exam Week Class Schedule, May 17-21, 2027</caption><thead><tr><th>Date and time</th><th>Monday may 17</th><th>Tuesday may 18</th><th>Wednesday may 19</th><th>Thursday may 20</th><th>Friday may 21</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>8:00 am - 10:30 am</td><td>8:00 MWF</td><td>8:30 Tu Th</td><td>9 MWF</td><td>10:00 Tu Th</td><td>10:00 MWF</td></tr><tr><td>11:00 am - 1:30 pm</td><td>11:00 MWF</td><td>11:30 Tu Th</td><td>12 MWF</td><td>1:00 Tu Th</td><td>1:00 MWF</td></tr><tr><td>2:00 pm - 4:30 pm</td><td>2:00 MWF</td><td>2:30 Tu Th</td><td>4 MWF</td><td>4:00 Tu Th</td><td>--</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>&nbsp;</h4><p>Note:All one-day-a-week evening classes (Starting at 5:00 pm or later only) will meet at their regularly scheduled times.</p><h4>&nbsp;Instructions for determining when your Final Exam is scheduled:</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id="e89f39524ece12832a1dc2ecb89021a8e">Final Exam times are determined by the meeting time of your class. For example, if your class meets 10 Tu Th your final exam will be on Thursday, May 20 from 8:00 to 10:30 am. Courses with labs are scheduled based on the lecture time of the course.</li><li data-list-item-id="e99b358b5dede6530fed4997ec8cca4dd">Courses which do not follow a standard time pattern are scheduled based on the initial schedule time of the course. For example, a course which is scheduled to meet at 2 on WThF has an initial meeting time of 2W. The only 2W on the chart is on Monday, May 17. Therefore, the final for a course which meets 2 WThF is scheduled for Monday, May 17 from 2:00 to 4:30 pm.</li><li data-list-item-id="eea7685befc41d48bf29cdf650f85aba8">Final Exams for in-person classes are held in regularly assigned rooms.</li></ul><p><strong>Students should consult the Finals Week schedule to avoid enrolling in courses which would cause them to have multiple examinations on the same day.</strong></p>
              </div>
              
              <div class="d-flex gap-2 justify-content-start align-items-center my-1">
                            </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
          </div>
      <div class="d-flex gap-2 justify-content-center align-items-center my-3">
      </div>
  </div>


